From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: rockchip: rk2 - Add GCM for AES and SM4

The crypto v2 engine computes GCM itself: it takes the associated data
and the text as one DMA list of two items, the associated data first and
marked as such, builds the counter from the 12-byte IV, and leaves the
tag in its tag registers. Rockchip's kernel drives gcm(aes) and gcm(sm4)
this way; the engine's version register offers the mode as bit 8.

Copy a request's associated data and text into one coherent buffer, run
that list, and copy the text and the tag back, checking the tag on
decryption. A request without associated data or text, or larger than
the buffer, goes to the software fallback, as Rockchip's kernel sends it.
AES ranks under the CPU's GCM and SM4 over the generic one, as the
driver ranks its other modes.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
